# Issue #178 — ProcessIR entry-point diagnostic parity

## Decision record

### 1. Validation policy: unconditional parser revalidation, policy remains semantic-only

Choose the third option: phase-separated validation.

- Keep `parse_process_ir_v1(payload: Any) -> ProcessIRV1` unchanged. Do not add `validation_policy`.
- Every direct `compile_process_ir_v1(...)` call, including policy-bearing legacy calls, must first serialize the supplied mutable model with `model_dump(mode="json", warnings=False)` and reparse it strictly.
- `LegacyValidationPolicyV1` continues to apply only after CFG lowering, when `_enforce_semantic_report` reclassifies named semantic findings.
- A parser-invalid legacy model is therefore refused with the parser’s diagnostic even when a legacy policy is supplied. Legacy callers retain their deliberate semantic exemptions, but no longer retain divergent grammar diagnostics.

Evidence:

- ProcessIR models are mutable because `_ProcessIRBase` forbids extras but is not frozen: [process_ir.py](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/models/process_ir.py:190), lines 190–194.
- The parser’s complete gate—payload shape, secret scan, version, Pydantic grammar, and whole-document rules—is [parse_process_ir_v1](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/models/process_ir.py:2743), lines 2743–2784.
- Policies are explicitly adapter-owned and unavailable to general validation: [validation_policy.py](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/compiler/process_ir/semantic_validation/validation_policy.py:18), lines 18–29.
- The four policy mappings are post-lowering semantic codes only, at lines 53–69; `apply_policy` merely reclassifies `ValidationReportV1.errors`, at lines 158–192.
- Policy is currently applied after `validate_lowered_process_ir`: [pipeline.py](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/compiler/process_ir/pipeline.py:82), lines 82–133.
- All shipped adapters already construct their IR through strict parsing: `_process_ir_compat.py` lines 676–759 and 850–893, `sync_pipeline.py` lines 404–425, and `wrapper_subprocess.py` lines 103–133.
- A read-only probe over 27 committed legacy specimens found 27 strict dump/reparse successes with exact JSON equality; three still required their semantic policy to compile. This demonstrates that strict grammar validation and legacy semantic exemption coexist.

Rejected alternatives:

- Adding policy to the parser would broaden an adapter-only exemption surface without any parser diagnostic that the policy can currently exempt.
- Skipping the reparse when `validation_policy is not None` would preserve the mutable-model hole this issue is meant to close.
- Extracting a shared compiler-wide precedence chain is unnecessary for #178 and remains a possible part of #154’s matrix derivation work.

### 2. Diagnostic authority: the parser

The parser is authoritative for diagnostic identity whenever the serialized model is parser-refused.

Public contract:

- `parse_process_ir_v1` continues to raise `ProcessIRValidationError`.
- `compile_process_ir_v1` converts the same parser findings to `ProcessIRCompileError`, preserving the complete ordered `(code, JSON pointer, message)` vector verbatim. Preserve remediation too; set `phase="schema"` and derive `node_identity` from the pointer.
- Compiler stages consume the fresh reparsed model, not the caller-owned model that was merely checked.
- Parser refusal happens before `validate_body_capabilities`, lowering, invariants, semantic validation, or emission.
- Unexpected dump/parser failures become the existing value-free `PROCESS_IR_COMPILE_INTERNAL` schema diagnostic.

The parser owns authored grammar and whole-document ordering; the compiler still owns parser-accepted documents’ CFG, references, lineage, and emission diagnostics. “Acceptance symmetry” in this slice therefore means grammar acceptance at the compile entry, not that the schema parser promises to accept every document that may later fail symbol-aware semantic compilation.

No `src/` consumer branches on the superseded compiler diagnostic for these malformed documents; the only intentional pin is the test discussed below.

