## Risks / open questions

- No blocking design question remains.
- The safety test is intentionally scoped to parser-owned grammar. Full compilation may legitimately reject a parser-valid document for symbol, CFG, lineage, or capability reasons.
- The node palette is manually constructed once per grammar kind, but exact equality with the parser-derived vocabulary prevents silent drift; cases themselves are fully generated.
- `BODY_CAPABILITIES_V1` remains a manually maintained authority. This plan tests all of it but does not derive it from model unions; #154 item 6 owns that change.
- Linear root length is unbounded, so no absolute performance ceiling can be claimed. The implementation should record the measured linear bound and call counts, not add a brittle latency threshold.
- The private compile core is a potential internal bypass if later reused incorrectly. Keep it non-exported, call it only immediately after `_parse_payload_for_compile`, and pin that every public direct compile reaches `_reparse_process_ir_for_compile`.
